# Anchored literal paths only, following `rust-rules/.gitignore`'s convention rather than
# arriving at it by accident.
#
# The component this module ships is *not* ignored and is not written here: `just go-rules`
# builds it into `crates/lanekeep-rules/components/`, where it is committed alongside the
# Rust- and TypeScript-authored ones, because `crates/lanekeep-rules` embeds it with
# `include_bytes!` and no gate may require TinyGo. The generated bindings under `internal/`
# are committed too, for the same reason: `wit-bindgen-go` is deterministic, and committing
# its output keeps `just check` free of a Go toolchain entirely.
#
# What is left is what a person produces by hand while working on a rule — a one-off
# `tinygo build -o …` at the module root, which should never reach a commit.
/out.wasm
/rule.wasm
/go-builtins.wasm
